Z||000013||kslish||05-16-2001||08:48 PM||||The Matrix has to be my favorite movie of all time.  I love a movie that freeks you out by making you think.<P>I'm trying to think of other movies...there is so many I can't really form a small list.  A lot of the good ones have already been mentioned Godfather, LeMans...I'd also add Friday, Smokey & the Bandit, Batman (only the Michael Keaton ones), the original Star Wars trilogy (Episode 1 was a dissapointment in my book) plus a ton more I can't think of right now.<P>Oh yeah, Jackie Chan movies just for the stunts, Clint Eastwood movies for Westerns (especially The Unforgiven) and Pulp Fiction since I had to watch it a few times just to piece it all together (I liked the challenge).<P>One movie that will definately not make my all time list is Titanic.  It's an okay movie but I was sort of disappointed after seeing it.  Probably because of all the hype that surrounded it when it was out.  <P>Ken S.<p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 05-16-2001).]||||reg||1
