Z||000032||Jay||05-17-2001||04:46 PM||||Moothergoose, I'm not talking down and I don't love violence.  I just think that a good story is better than a guy getting kicked in the balls! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  After all, there is very little violence in all three Godfather movies (Sunny's death, heads of the 5 families, Fredo).  For me (and I'm only speaking about myself here) I want to see character developement.  I want to feel like I know the people on screen, feel what they are feeling.  I come away from a movie like that more satisfied that I haven't just wasted a few hours of my time and money watching some guy take one to the mid section.  But I have to admit that I love Monty Python which is the epitome of stupid humor.  But even Monty Python makes fun of social, political and religious material.  I think what I'm trying to say is that there is nothing wrong with "Big Daddy" type movies, but for me, they aren't comparable to movies like "Malcolm X", "Do the Right Thing", "Color Purple", "Usual Suspect" ect.<BR>Don't get me wrong I've watched my share of comedies (I'm gonna get you sucka, Kings of Comedy,Friday, Vacation ect), and I'm not taking offense to your statement.  Just thought I should clear up my view on the matter.  Substance is not relative.  Movies have the power to make us laugh and cry and every emotion in between.  Every movie has substance depending on what frame of mind you go into it with.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande||||reg||1
Z||000033||JSocha||05-17-2001||05:15 PM||||Jay, man....that was deep!<P>For sure, you must be a full blooded Canadian!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
